  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">People&apos;s Recovery FTC project_CPD</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The major context of this programme is the continuation of the global Covid-19 pandemic and its devastating impact on people throughout the world. Most countries are still struggling with dealing with the healthcare crisis engendered by the pandemic, and consequently, have yet to or are still tackling its deleterious effects on the economy. This work is part of a wider FTC project. The activities are: - Qualitative and quantitative analysis of covid-19 policy responses in Bangladesh. - Using an updated methodology to take account of new ways to understand gender impacts of policies. - Providing summary reports of country case studies. - Contributing to a global report on the &apos;people&apos;s recovery&apos;. - Disseminating the global report and other relevant policy products. - Engaging in and supporting relevant advocacy at national and regional levels. As with the first report, most global trackers have focused especially on the economic impacts, or the health impacts of the pandemic. It remains a task of vital importance to highlight the link between the two, and this project is a contribution towards this understanding</narrative>
  </description>
